</style>
<div id="cards"></div>
<button id="send" style="font-size:14px;padding:8px 14px">Send my answers for a verdict</button>
</div>
<script>
const Q=[
["1. Rank by SN2 rate (fastest first): 1-bromobutane, 2-bromobutane, 2-bromo-2-methylpropane.",
["From which side must the nucleophile approach the carbon bearing Br? Count the carbon groups attached to that carbon in each compound.",
"Parallel case: for chlorides, methyl chloride reacts faster than ethyl chloride, which reacts faster than isopropyl chloride. What trend is that, and where do your three fall?"]],
["2. Which is the better leaving group, Cl- or I-? Why?",
["A good leaving group is a stable anion that is comfortable holding the electron pair. What does the strength of the conjugate acid tell you about that?",
"Parallel case: HBr is a stronger acid than HCl, and Br- is a better leaving group than Cl-. Extend the series, and think about anion size and charge spread."]],
["3. Predict the product of sodium ethoxide with iodomethane.",
["Label the nucleophile and the electrophile. Which atom attacks which carbon, and what leaves?",
"Parallel case: hydroxide + chloromethane gives methanol. Swap in your nucleophile and leaving group, and write the new bond."]],
["4. Why does DMSO speed up SN2 compared with methanol?",
["Ask what each solvent does to the anionic nucleophile: which one has an O-H or N-H available to interact with it, and which one doesn't?",
"Parallel case: in water, fluoride is a weak nucleophile because water molecules cage it. What happens to a nucleophile that isn't caged?"]],
["5. What happens to the stereocenter in (R)-2-bromobutane with NaCN?",
["Combine two things: SN2 attacks from the side opposite the leaving group, and the other three groups are left behind. What does that do to the shape?",
"Parallel case: an umbrella blowing inside out. Then ask whether the label R or S must change, and say how you'd check using priorities."]]];
const cards=document.getElementById('cards');
Q.forEach((q,i)=>{
 const d=document.createElement('div');d.className='c';
 d.innerHTML=`<p>${q[0]}</p><textarea id="a${i}" placeholder="Your answer and reasoning"></textarea>
 <button data-i="${i}">Hint</button><div class="h" id="h${i}"></div>`;
 cards.appendChild(d);
 let n=0;
 d.querySelector('button').onclick=e=>{
  const h=document.getElementById('h'+i);
  if(n<2){h.style.display='block';h.innerHTML+=(n?'<br><br>':'')+'Hint '+(n+1)+': '+q[1][n];n++;
   e.target.textContent=n<2?'Another hint':'No more hints';}
 };
});
document.getElementById('send').onclick=()=>{
 let t="Here are my answers to the SN2 practice set:\n";
 Q.forEach((q,i)=>{t+=`\n${i+1}. ${document.getElementById('a'+i).value||'(no answer yet)'}`});
 sendPrompt(t);
};
</script>
